Nitrogen dioxide reacts with ozone to form Dinitrogen Pentoxide and Oxygen. The reaction can be represented as.
$2 \mathrm{NO}_2(\mathrm{~g})+\mathrm{O}_3(\mathrm{~g}) \rightarrow \mathrm{N}_2 \mathrm{O}_5(\mathrm{~g})+\mathrm{O}_2(\mathrm{~g})$
Experimentally the overall rate of the reaction was found to be first order in both $\mathrm{NO}_2$ as well as $\mathrm{O}_3$ i.e. rate $=\mathrm{K}\left[\mathrm{NO}_2\right]  \left[\mathrm{O}_3\right]$ Mechanism I:
\begin{gathered}
\mathrm{NO}}_{2}+\mathrm{O}_3 \rightarrow \mathrm{NO}_3+\mathrm{O}_2 \text { Slow } \\
\mathrm{NO}_3+\mathrm{NO}_2 \rightarrow \mathrm{~N}_2 \mathrm{O}_5 \text { Fast }
\end{gathered}$
Mechanism II :
\begin{gathered}
\mathrm{O}}_{3} \rightleftharpoons \mathrm{O}_2+\mathrm{O} \text { Fast } \\
\mathrm{NO}_2+\mathrm{O} \rightarrow \mathrm{NO}_3 \text { Slow } \\
\mathrm{NO}_3+\mathrm{NO}_2 \rightarrow \mathrm{~N}_2 \mathrm{O}_5 \text { Fast }
\end{gathered} Which of the following are correct?$
